        "original_id": "7e844757-8df4-5ac0-bb19-e2bb3adc1383",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Wilfrid Brambell, Harry H. Corbett, Paul McCartney, Ray Galton, Alan Simpson\n- Works: Steptoe and Son Ride Again, A Hard Day's Night, Some Will, Some Won't, Get Well Soon, Steptoe and Son\n- Concepts: cameo roles, fictional characters, TV writers, tuberculosis sanatorium\n\nFacts:\n- In 1947, Ray Galton and Alan Simpson, the writers of Steptoe and Son, met in a tuberculosis sanatorium, and Get Well Soon was based on that meeting.\n- Wilfrid Brambell appeared alongside the Beatles in A Hard Day's Night, playing Paul McCartney's fictional grandfather.\n- Wilfrid Brambell had a cameo role in Some Will, Some Won't as Henry Russell, who left four family members £150,000 in his will on the condition that they complete bizarre tasks.\n- Steptoe and Son Ride Again again starred Wilfrid Brambell and Harry H. Corbett.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
